  "notes": "'Dum' means steaming sealed: the chicken cooks in its own marinade while the rice finishes in the steam.\nThe fried onions are the soul of the dish; bought crispy onions work in a pinch.\n\nHealthier swap: fry the onions in the air fryer with 2 tbsp oil, use boneless skinless thighs, skip the ghee and serve with a big cucumber raita made with Skyr.\n\nNutrition is estimated.",
