  "notes": "What matters most:\n1. Rice: day-old, cold and dry. Fresh rice? Spread it on a tray and chill uncovered for 1 hour.\n2. Heat: as hot as your stove goes. Work in batches of max. 2 portions so the wok stays hot.\n3. Seasoning: mostly salt and white pepper. Too much soy makes it brown and soggy.\n4. Egg: scramble first and add back at the end, so it stays fluffy.\nPro trick: for 'golden fried rice', mix 2 raw yolks into the rice before frying.\n\nHealthier swap: 1.5 tbsp oil, double the veg, add prawns or chicken for protein.\n\nNutrition is estimated.",
