   "Homemade spätzle (optional): beat flour, eggs, salt, nutmeg and water with a wooden spoon until the dough is thick, smooth and bubbly. Rest 10 minutes. Grate it through your spätzle grater into boiling salted water in batches and lift out as soon as they float.",
   "Bought spätzle: warm them in boiling salted water or in a pan with a little butter.",
   "Heat the oven to 180 °C. Layer the hot spätzle and cheese in a warm baking dish with lots of pepper. Add a ladle of cooking water to keep it creamy.",
   "Bake for 5 to 10 minutes until the cheese melts into strings.",
   "Pile the crispy onions and chives on top and serve with a green salad."
